<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="63855" href="schedule/2015/fall/RST/199/63855.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120158" href="schedule/2015/fall.xml">Fall 2015</term><subject id="RST" href="schedule/2015/fall/RST.xml">Recreation, Sport, and Tourism</subject><course id="199" href="schedule/2015/fall/RST/199.xml">Undergraduate Open Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>ONB</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Disability in RST</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 19-Oct-15 - 09-Dec-15.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course will examine the different aspects of disability in the recreation, sport, and tourism industries. Physical and mental disabilities will be discussed as well as their applications to each field. Specifically, the class will examine such topics as disability culture (activities, sports, vacation planning), technology, participation, accessibility, and barriers.</sectionText><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-10-19Z</startDate><endDate>2015-12-09Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="ONL">Online</type><start>ARRANGED</start><instructors><instructor lastName="Ruddell" firstName="J">Ruddell, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>